{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-exo-3-1","title":"Exodus 3:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Moses keeps Jethro's flock. 2 God appears to him in a burning bush. 9 He sends him to deliver Israel. 13 The name of God. 15 His message to Israel, and Pharaoh, whose opposition is foretold. 20 He is assured of Israel's deliverance.</p>\n<p>A.M. 2513. B.C. 1491. kept. Ps 78:70-72; Am 1:1; 7:14,15; Mt 4:18,19; Lu 2:8 his father. 2:16,21; 18:1-6; Nu 10:29; Jud 4:11 the mountain. 5; 18:5; 19:3,11; 24:15-17; 1Ki 19:8 Horeb. 17:6; De 1:6; 4:10; Ps 106:19; Mal 4:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-3-2","title":"Exodus 3:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>angel. 4,6; Ge 16:7-13; 22:15,16; 48:16; De 33:16; Isa 63:9; Ho 12:4,5 Mal 3:1; Lu 20:37; Ac 7:30-35 bush burned. Ge 15:13-17; De 4:20; Ps 66:12; Isa 43:2; 53:10,11; Da 3:27 Zec 13:7; Joh 1:14; Ro 8:3; 2Co 1:8-10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-3-3","title":"Exodus 3:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Job 37:14; Ps 107:8; 111:2-4; Ac 7:31</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-3-4","title":"Exodus 3:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>unto him. De 33:16 Moses. Ge 22:1,11; 46:2; 1Sa 3:4,6,8,10; Ps 62:11; Ac 9:4; 10:3,13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-3-5","title":"Exodus 3:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>Draw not. 19:12,21; Le 10:3; Heb 12:20 put off. Ge 28:16,17; Jos 5:15; Ec 5:1; Ac 7:33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-3-6","title":"Exodus 3:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>I am. 14,15; 4:5; 29:45; Ge 12:1,7; 17:7,8; 26:24; 28:13; 31:42; 32:9 1Ki 18:36; Es 3:4; Ps 132:2; Jer 24:7; 31:33; 32:38; Eze 11:20 Zec 8:8; Mt 22:32; Mr 12:26; Lu 20:37; Ac 7:32,32 thy father.Though the word {avicha,} \"thy father,\" is here used in the singular, yet St. Stephen, quoting this passage (Ac. 7:32), uses the plural, [Lo Theos ton patron sou,] \"the God of thy fathers;\" and that this is the meaning, the following words prove. This reading is confirmed by the Samaritan and Coptic.</p>\n<p>hid. Ge 17:3; Jud 13:22; 1Ki 19:13; Ne 9:9; Job 42:5,6; Ps 106:44,45 Isa 6:1-5; Da 10:7,8; Mt 17:6; Lu 5:8; Ac 7:34; Heb 12:21; Re 1:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-3-7","title":"Exodus 3:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>I have. 2:23-25; 22:23; Ge 29:32; 1Sa 9:16; Ps 22:24; 34:4,6; 106:44 Ps 145:19; Isa 63:9; Heb 4:15 by reason. 1:11 I know. Ge 18:21; Ps 142:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-3-8","title":"Exodus 3:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>I am. Ge 11:5,7; 18:21; 50:24; Ps 18:9-19; 12:5; 22:4,5; 34:8; 91:15 Isa 64:1; Joh 3:13; 6:38 deliver. 6:6-8; 12:51; Ge 15:14; 50:24 unto a good. 17; 13:5; 33:2,3; Ge 13:14,15; 15:18; Nu 13:19,27; 14:7,8; De 1:7,25 De 8:7-9; 11:9-24; 26:9-15; 27:3; 28:11; Ne 9:22-25; Jer 2:7; 11:5 Jer 32:22; Eze 20:6 Canaanites. 22:23-31; 34:11; Ge 15:18-21; De 7:1; Jos 9:1; Ne 9:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-3-9","title":"Exodus 3:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>the cry. 7; 2:23 and I have. 7; 1:11,13,14,22; Ps 12:5; Pr 22:22,23; Ec 4:1; 5:8; Jer 50:33,34 Am 4:1; Mic 2:1-3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-3-10","title":"Exodus 3:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>1Sa 12:6; Ps 77:20; 103:6,7; 105:26; Isa 63:11,12; Ho 12:13 Mic 6:4; Ac 7:34,36</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-3-11","title":"Exodus 3:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>4:10-13; 6:12; 1Sa 18:18; 2Sa 7:18; 1Ki 3:7,9; Isa 6:5-8; Jer 1:6 Ac 7:23-25; 2Co 2:16; 3:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-3-12","title":"Exodus 3:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>Certainly. 4:12,15; Ge 15:1; 31:3; De 31:23; Jos 1:5; Isa 41:10; 43:2; Mt 28:20 Mr 16:20; Ac 11:21; Ro 8:31; Heb 13:5 token. 4:1-9; Ge 15:8; Jud 6:17,21,36-40; 7:11,13,14; Ps 86:17; Isa 7:14 Isa 37:30; Jer 43:9,10; 51:63,64 ye shall. 19:1-40:38; Le 1:1-27:34; Nu 1:1-10:36</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-3-13","title":"Exodus 3:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>What is his name. 14; 15:3; Ge 32:29; Jud 13:6,17; Pr 30:4; Isa 7:14; 9:6; Jer 23:6 Mt 1:21,23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-3-14","title":"Exodus 3:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>I AM hath. 6:3; Job 11:7; Ps 68:4; 90:2; Isa 44:6; Mt 18:20; 28:20; Joh 8:58 2Co 1:20; Heb 13:8; Re 1:4,8,17; 4:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-3-15","title":"Exodus 3:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>The Lord. 6; 4:5; Ge 17:7,8; De 1:11,35; 4:1; 2Ch 28:9; Mt 22:32; Ac 7:32 this is my name for ever.The name here referred to is that which immediately precedes, [yhwh,] ,] {Yehowah,} which we translate \"Lord\", the name by which God had been known from the creation of the world, (Ge 2:2,) and by which he is known to the present day. [yhwh,] {Yehowah,} from [hwh,] {hawah,} to be, subsist, signifies \"He who is\", or \"subsists\", i.e., eminently and in a manner superior to all other beings; and is essentially the same with [ahwh,] {eheyeh,} \"I AM\", in the preceding verse.</p>\n<p>Ps 72:17,19; 135:13; 145:1,2; Isa 9:6; 63:12 my memorial. Ps 102:12; Ho 12:5; Mic 4:5; Mal 3:6; Heb 13:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-3-16","title":"Exodus 3:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>elders. 4:29; 18:12; 24:11; Ge 1:7; Mt 26:3; Ac 11:30; 20:17; 1Pe 5:1 visited. 2:25; 4:31; 13:19; 15:14; Ge 21:1; 50:24; Ru 1:6; Ps 8:4; Lu 1:68 Lu 19:44; Ac 15:14; Heb 2:6,7; 1Pe 2:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-3-17","title":"Exodus 3:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>I will bring. 9; 2:23-25; Ge 15:13-21; 46:4; 50:24 unto the land. 8; Ge 15:14,18-21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-3-18","title":"Exodus 3:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>and they. 16; 4:31; Jos 1:17; 2Ch 30:12; Ps 110:3; Jer 26:5 and thou. 5:1-3 The Lord. 7:16; 9:1,13; 10:3 met. 4:24; 5:3; 25:22; 29:42,43; 30:6,36; Ge 12:1; 15:1; 17:1; 48:3 Nu 17:4; 23:3,4,15,16; Isa 64:5 three days'. 8:27; 13:17,18 that we may. 12; 7:16; 8:25-28; 9:1; 10:24-26; 19:1; Jer 2:2,6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-3-19","title":"Exodus 3:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>will not. 5:2; 7:4 no, not by a mighty hand. or, but by a strong hand. 6:1; 7:1-14:31; Ps 136:11,12; Isa 63:12,13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-3-20","title":"Exodus 3:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>stretch. 6:6; 7:5; 9:15; Eze 20:33 smite. 7:3; 11:9; De 4:34; 6:22; Ne 9:10; Ps 105:27; 106:22; 135:8,9 Isa 19:22; Jer 32:20,21; Ac 7:36 See chapters Ac 7:1-13:42 after that. 11:8; 12:31,39; Ge 15:14; Jud 6:8; 8:16; Isa 26:11; Ps 105:38</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-3-21","title":"Exodus 3:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>11:3; 12:36; Ge 39:21; Ne 1:11; Ps 106:46; Pr 16:7; Ac 7:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-3-22","title":"Exodus 3:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>But. 11:2; 12:35,36; Ge 15:14; Ps 105:37 borrow.Or, rather ask or demand, as the word [sh�'al ] properly signifies; and is so rendered by the LXX., Vulgate, and Geneva and Barker's Bible: the other ancient versions are the same as the Hebrew.</p>\n<p>spoil. Job 27:16,17; Pr 13:22; Isa 33:1; Eze 39:10 the Egyptians. or, Egypt.</p>"}]}